From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reilly Brogan <reilly@reillybrogan.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] pam: Apply limits to the systemd user manager

The systemd-user PAM stack does not include pam_limits, so limits set in
limits.conf or limits.d (for example rtprio/memlock for a realtime group)
never reach user@.service or the applications it launches.

Origin: vendor
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-02
---
 src/login/systemd-user.in | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/login/systemd-user.in b/src/login/systemd-user.in
--- a/src/login/systemd-user.in
+++ b/src/login/systemd-user.in
@@ -15,6 +15,7 @@
 session  required   pam_loginuid.so
 session  optional   pam_keyinit.so force revoke
 session  required   pam_namespace.so
+session  required   pam_limits.so
 {% if ENABLE_HOMED %}
 -session optional   pam_systemd_home.so
 {% endif %}
